sql-migration-review:
Review this migration before I run it on production, the orders table has 80 million rows:
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN status text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'new';
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_status ON orders (status);

Is this migration safe? Postgres 15, table users has about 12 million rows.
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN legacy_id;
ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN email SET NOT NULL;

Check this down migration for me, I want to be sure it will not lose data:
DROP TABLE payments_archive;
ALTER TABLE payments RENAME COLUMN amount_cents TO amount;

Look at this migration and tell me what could lock the table:
ALTER TABLE events ADD CONSTRAINT fk_events_user FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id);
CREATE INDEX ON events (created_at);
